From 046476afbf82e3b10901619456ed1847c0a9dae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:31:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] NAOMI port, first stage: boot, JVS controls, live figures

ports/naomi: the game, its board and its sound program on a NAOMI's SH-4
(KallistiOS, KOS_SUBARCH=naomi), the Crazy Taxi upright's wheel, pedals and
two-position shifter through the JVS, video.c drawn every few frames into a
framebuffer, and the time each part takes for the netbooter's Raspberry to
peek at (live.py). naomi_assets.py makes the NAOMI's pack (tiles two pens to a
byte, samples apart: 21.6 MB). The NetDIMM files, peeks and console ring come
from the NAOMI build of Daytona USA's native port.

runtime: tasks on the SH-4 (registers on the task's stack, as on aarch64;
TASK_STACK_SIZE settable), ORUNNERS_PACKED_PENS for the packed tiles (same
video hashes as the normal build over 3,501 frames).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016VRYRPP2crYKhAiGSakTbz
