From 3d5d3349ae774a770c1b47d6550b508b42237d79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:12:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] NAOMI port runs on the board: game thread with the tasks'
 stacks, faster sound board

Found on the NAOMI 2 through the NetDIMM: KallistiOS stops a thread whose
stack pointer is below its stack's base, so the game now runs in a thread
whose stack holds the tasks' stacks (host_task_area). 64-bit divisions in the
sound board's time conversions replaced with exact 32-bit ones, FM synthesis
off (OutRunners plays no FM note), the sound hashes and the hidden screen's
sprite erase off (ORUNNERS_NAOMI): ~8 ms of game and ~2.9 ms of sound a frame.
video.c's state from the heap. Exception handler that keeps answering peeks,
a sampling profiler, watch.py and profile.py, test stages.

