From b397cb0c36115227ac32196a0657a98e71d8ab9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:17:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] NAOMI stage 2: the frame on the PowerVR2 (scene of
 textured quads)

runtime/src/video_scene.c (ORUNNERS_VIDEO_SCENE, included by video.c): the
frame as textured quads for a GPU: tilemap pages and the text map as images
redrawn where cells or colours change, NBG0 split where it crosses pages,
NBG2 line by line (row scroll, row select), the bitmap layer through window 4,
the backdrop, sprites from a cache of images in their colours, the mixer's
priorities as depth, colour offsets as modulate and add. Checked against
video.c with video_scene_soft.c (ORUNNERS_SCENE_COMPARE in the headless
build): most frames under 1 % of pixels differ (sprite edges); fades are an
approximation.

ports/naomi/pvr_video.c: the images as ARGB1555 textures, the quads as
punch-through polygons sent by direct rendering, sorted by texture. On the
board: 60 fps in attract and most of a race. Also: misaligned loads and
stores done a byte at a time in the exception handler (the V60's code reads
words at odd addresses), MultiPCM synthesis off until the AICA plays it
(ORUNNERS_NO_PCM_SYNTHESIS), test inputs pokeable for races without anyone
at the cabinet (race.py).

